# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets headers.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# Strategy:
#   - COOP = same-origin-allow-popups, NO COEP. Room 3.0 OPFS uses OpfsSAHPoolDb
#     (SAH Pool VFS) which does not require SharedArrayBuffer, so COEP stays off
#     (adding it would gate SAB and break third-party scripts). COOP is NOT left
#     unset: Chromium tightened the opener↔popup relationship, and with an unset
#     (unsafe-none) opener the Firebase Auth popup's window.close() is blocked
#     ("Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy policy would block the window.close call"),
#     so signInWithPopup never delivers the credential and login silently fails.
#     `same-origin-allow-popups` restores the opener relationship for popups this
#     page opens (Firebase Auth, Stripe) while keeping cross-origin isolation off.
#     Official Firebase remedy (firebase-js-sdk#8541). Do NOT add COEP here.
#   - Hashed assets (wasm, chunk JS) → 1 year, immutable.
#   - Entry points (index.html, composeApp.js, init.js) → always revalidate.
#   - Compose resources (fixed names) → 1 day with revalidation.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups

/*.wasm
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Content-Type: application/wasm

/composeApp.*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/composeApp.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/init.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# NOTE: .cvr (Compose Value Resources) durability is enforced in index.html,
# NOT here. A corrupted/stale .cvr halts Compose rendering (Base64 decode crash
# → splash hang). index.html's fetch wrapper forces `cache: 'reload'` for every
# .cvr request, so they are always network-fresh regardless of this max-age.
# Do NOT add a separate `.cvr` rule here: Cloudflare _headers ACCUMULATES headers
# across all matching rules and JOINS duplicate header names with a comma, so a
# `.cvr` file would match both rules and emit a self-contradictory
# `Cache-Control: no-store, public, max-age=86400, ...` (unreliable in browsers).
/composeResources/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
